# Valgrind suppressions for the valgrind job in .github/workflows/native-checks.yaml.
#
# tools/ is in .Rbuildignore, so nothing here reaches the tarball or CRAN.
#
# One entry, and it is not this package's memory. R's iconv() builtin asks
# R_AllocStringBuffer for a growable buffer and never hands it back; R does
# not free on exit, so valgrind reports the block as definitely lost with a
# stack that is twelve frames of R with no zuxml frame anywhere in it. Any
# package whose tests convert an encoding sees the same block.
#
# Written against the whole call path rather than fun:malloc alone, so it
# suppresses this one allocation site and stays silent if a real leak ever
# appears under a different caller.
{
   R-do_iconv-R_AllocStringBuffer-never-freed
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:R_AllocStringBuffer
   fun:do_iconv
}
